3. Request vandhaa: Hello vs Data Store

Case A: Ippo irukka "Hello" code ☁️❌

Browser ──GET localhost:3000/server/entry_api/──▶ catalyst serve (laptop)
                                                    │
                                                    ▼
                                         index.js run (un laptop Node)
                                         res.write('Hello')
Browser ◀──────────── Hello ──────────────────────┘
Cloud ku oru request kooda pogaadhu. Idhu full ah offline ah ododum (startup check thavira). Ippo un index.js SDK use pannala, adhanaala.

Case B: Apram Data Store code ezhudhum bodhu ☁️✅

const catalyst = require('zcatalyst-sdk-node')
const app = catalyst.initialize(req)
await app.datastore().table('ParkingEntries').insertRow({...})

Browser ──POST──▶ catalyst serve (laptop :3000)
                     │ ① req kulla special headers inject pannum:
                     │    project ID, env, domain, access token
                     ▼
                  index.js (laptop la odudhu)
                     │ ② catalyst.initialize(req) → andha headers-a padikkum
                     │ ③ insertRow() → HTTPS call:
                     ▼
            ☁️ https://api.catalyst.zoho.in/baas/v1/project/50225000000046075/table/.../row
                     │   (Authorization: un access token)
                     ▼
            ☁️ Development Data Store → row save aagum
                     │
Browser ◀── response ┘

Key point: catalyst.initialize(req) ku req yen kudukkurom nu ippo puriyum. catalyst serve (local) or Catalyst cloud (deploy aanadhum), rendum req kulla project/auth details vechu anuppum. SDK adha eduthu dhaan cloud kooda pesum. Nee code la project ID, password edhuvum ezhudha vendaam.

